1
00:00:05,505 --> 00:00:08,632
Read forwards or backwards,
my name is Minami Minamida.

2
00:00:08,633 --> 00:00:10,134
<i>Autism Spectrum Disorder?</i>

3
00:00:10,135 --> 00:00:11,927
Her background isn't bad, right?

4
00:00:11,928 --> 00:00:13,762
If she isn't at the level
to stand in court,

5
00:00:13,763 --> 00:00:15,639
<i>will you reconsider her employment?</i>

6
00:00:15,640 --> 00:00:16,890
You did it! See?

7
00:00:16,891 --> 00:00:19,268
<i>The victim died while being transported.</i>

8
00:00:19,269 --> 00:00:20,853
Maybe being a lawyer

9
00:00:20,854 --> 00:00:23,063
<i>was impossible for me
with autism after all.</i>

10
00:00:23,064 --> 00:00:24,732
Unless the prosecution

11
00:00:24,733 --> 00:00:27,026
can medically prove a causal relationship

12
00:00:27,027 --> 00:00:29,903
<i>between the defendant's strike
and the resulting death,</i>

13
00:00:29,904 --> 00:00:33,074
the defendant cannot be held
criminally responsible!

14
00:00:35,660 --> 00:00:40,373
The time has come for the two of you
to take a step toward your new life.

15
00:00:40,915 --> 00:00:42,833
Please rise

16
00:00:42,834 --> 00:00:45,837
and give a big round of applause
for the bride and groom.

17
00:00:47,130 --> 00:00:49,549
The bride and groom
will now make their exit.

18
00:02:15,301 --> 00:02:18,262
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LPC
NEW ATTORNEY MINAMI MINAMIDA

19
00:02:18,263 --> 00:02:20,681
Don't push yourself. Use the stairs.

20
00:02:20,682 --> 00:02:23,600
- Good morning, Ms. Asahi.
- Morning.

21
00:02:23,601 --> 00:02:25,602
I'm waiting for someone right now.

22
00:02:25,603 --> 00:02:26,771
Someone?

23
00:02:27,397 --> 00:02:28,565
Talking about whales.

24
00:02:29,149 --> 00:02:30,984
Isn't it fine
when it's just the two of us?

25
00:02:32,110 --> 00:02:32,985
What?

26
00:02:32,986 --> 00:02:35,697
That's why I'm waiting here for Mr. Funai.

27
00:02:36,406 --> 00:02:38,657
What's going on with you two?

28
00:02:38,658 --> 00:02:40,409
ATTORNEY
TAKUMA HIMI

29
00:02:40,410 --> 00:02:42,203
Wouldn't Funai already be here?

30
00:02:43,329 --> 00:02:45,289
Good morning, Mr. Himi.

31
00:02:45,290 --> 00:02:47,333
If Mr. Funai is here, I'll go now.

32
00:02:48,626 --> 00:02:51,211
Good morning, Ms. Minamida.

33
00:02:51,212 --> 00:02:53,171
Good morning, Managing Partner.

34
00:02:53,172 --> 00:02:54,381
HIROKAWA - TSUCHIMURA

35
00:02:54,382 --> 00:02:57,093
How's work?
Take your time getting used to it.

36
00:02:57,760 --> 00:02:59,553
Yes, I'll take my time.

37
00:02:59,554 --> 00:03:02,639
Is the Managing Partner
greeting Ms. Minamida herself?

38
00:03:02,640 --> 00:03:04,099
No, it's a coincidence.

39
00:03:04,100 --> 00:03:05,642
If you ever need anything,

40
00:03:05,643 --> 00:03:07,185
just tell me.

41
00:03:07,186 --> 00:03:08,396
Anything?

42
00:03:10,565 --> 00:03:12,358
- Have a good one.
- You too.

43
00:03:20,408 --> 00:03:23,328
So Ms. Minamida
was raised by a single father.

44
00:03:25,705 --> 00:03:27,665
Managing Partner, they've arrived.

45
00:03:30,335 --> 00:03:32,795
We've been expecting you, Chairman.

46
00:03:33,588 --> 00:03:35,047
- See?
- It's been a while.

47
00:03:35,048 --> 00:03:36,798
Thank you for coming.

48
00:03:36,799 --> 00:03:39,302
I'm pretty sure that man is...

49
00:03:40,345 --> 00:03:42,347
How much do you think that wedding cost?

50
00:03:43,139 --> 00:03:45,849
I trusted those hotel guys
to provide top-tier service,

51
00:03:45,850 --> 00:03:47,309
and it cost 30 million yen!

52
00:03:47,310 --> 00:03:48,393
PARTNER ATTORNEY
MIYAJI

53
00:03:48,394 --> 00:03:50,187
Here is the breakdown.

54
00:03:50,188 --> 00:03:51,813
I'll send it via email later as well.

55
00:03:51,814 --> 00:03:53,982
I paid 30 million

56
00:03:53,983 --> 00:03:57,527
just to be completely humiliated
in front of a huge crowd of guests.

57
00:03:57,528 --> 00:03:59,530
I completely understand how you feel.

58
00:04:00,240 --> 00:04:03,409
So, how much can we get from the hotel?

59
00:04:05,411 --> 00:04:08,289
That man from earlier
is the Chairman of Kurasawa Food Systems.

60
00:04:09,415 --> 00:04:11,917
Apparently, his daughter had her wedding

61
00:04:11,918 --> 00:04:13,753
with the heir
of Mikoshiba Land Development,

62
00:04:14,629 --> 00:04:18,173
but her wedding dress slipped down
in the middle of the ceremony,

63
00:04:18,174 --> 00:04:21,386
leaving her fully exposed
in front of a huge crowd.

64
00:04:21,886 --> 00:04:22,887
So her underwear...

65
00:04:26,599 --> 00:04:27,517
Wow...

66
00:04:28,142 --> 00:04:29,018
Wow...

67
00:04:33,481 --> 00:04:35,440
- Welcome back, sir.
- Welcome back.

68
00:04:35,441 --> 00:04:36,859
I'm at my wits' end.

69
00:04:37,819 --> 00:04:40,362
That man from earlier,
he's from Kurasawa Food Systems--

70
00:04:40,363 --> 00:04:41,446
The Chairman, right?

71
00:04:41,447 --> 00:04:43,782
Mr. Himi was gossiping that his daughter's

72
00:04:43,783 --> 00:04:45,242
wedding dress slipped down.

73
00:04:45,243 --> 00:04:47,869
What? I-- I just happened to overhear it!

74
00:04:47,870 --> 00:04:51,665
But Kurasawa Food Systems isn't
one of our corporate clients, are they?

75
00:04:51,666 --> 00:04:55,502
Up until now, they had
a corporate retainer with MMK Law Firm.

76
00:04:55,503 --> 00:04:57,754
But MMK turned this case down,

77
00:04:57,755 --> 00:04:59,799
- so he came to us, their rival.
- And?

78
00:05:01,759 --> 00:05:03,969
The hotel offered a full refund
of the wedding costs

79
00:05:03,970 --> 00:05:06,888
plus hotel vouchers worth 5 million yen,

80
00:05:06,889 --> 00:05:08,640
but he said that isn't enough.

81
00:05:08,641 --> 00:05:10,642
I think that's not bad compensation.

82
00:05:10,643 --> 00:05:11,977
- Right?
- Yes.

83
00:05:11,978 --> 00:05:14,104
But he demands at least 100 million.

84
00:05:14,105 --> 00:05:15,272
100 million?

85
00:05:15,273 --> 00:05:18,650
The secretary emailed the details.
I'll forward them,

86
00:05:18,651 --> 00:05:20,110
- so take a look.
- What?

87
00:05:20,111 --> 00:05:21,528
Did you actually accept the case?

88
00:05:21,529 --> 00:05:22,780
Yeah.

89
00:05:23,323 --> 00:05:26,325
The Managing Partner got fired up

90
00:05:26,326 --> 00:05:28,910
the moment she heard MMK.

91
00:05:28,911 --> 00:05:30,329
What did you say just now?

92
00:05:30,330 --> 00:05:33,958
I said this place is just like MMK.

93
00:05:34,667 --> 00:05:36,334
You run away when a case

94
00:05:36,335 --> 00:05:38,588
is too big to handle. Am I wrong?

95
00:05:40,965 --> 00:05:43,884
The amount you want
is 100 million, correct?

96
00:05:43,885 --> 00:05:46,094
Understood. We'll take the case.

97
00:05:46,095 --> 00:05:47,180
Really?

98
00:05:47,680 --> 00:05:48,890
You'll do it!

99
00:05:49,474 --> 00:05:51,516
You really are different from MMK!

100
00:05:51,517 --> 00:05:52,518
Yes.

101
00:05:52,643 --> 00:05:55,979
Hirokawa & Howard LPC is on your side.

102
00:05:55,980 --> 00:05:59,650
HIROKAWA & HOWARD LPC
IS ON YOUR SIDE

103
00:06:03,196 --> 00:06:06,491
MANAGING PARTNER
NAGISA HIROKAWA

104
00:06:09,535 --> 00:06:10,452
So,

105
00:06:10,453 --> 00:06:13,455
let's all put our heads together
to figure out how to bill

106
00:06:13,456 --> 00:06:14,999
the hotel for 100 million.

107
00:06:16,250 --> 00:06:19,169
We can claim the roughly 30 million yen

108
00:06:19,170 --> 00:06:21,004
already paid for the wedding as damages,

109
00:06:21,005 --> 00:06:22,756
but we need to get the remaining

110
00:06:22,757 --> 00:06:24,674
70 million
out of emotional distress damages.

111
00:06:24,675 --> 00:06:28,011
In this case, 5 million
is the best we could do, right?

112
00:06:28,012 --> 00:06:30,514
It'd be different
if we had grounds to really increase

113
00:06:30,515 --> 00:06:31,890
the emotional distress damages.

114
00:06:31,891 --> 00:06:34,810
Apparently, the bride herself
says the dress was weird.

115
00:06:34,811 --> 00:06:37,020
The dress was a rental, right?

116
00:06:37,021 --> 00:06:39,064
If there was a problem with the dress,

117
00:06:39,065 --> 00:06:41,567
we can hold the hotel responsible
since they arranged it.

118
00:06:42,235 --> 00:06:44,361
Assuming there was gross negligence,

119
00:06:44,362 --> 00:06:46,571
the hotel will likely try to hide it.

120
00:06:46,572 --> 00:06:49,617
DESIRED CLAIM AMOUNT
FROM HOTEL: MINIMUM 100 MILLION

121
00:06:50,785 --> 00:06:52,994
Let's go undercover for this one.

122
00:06:52,995 --> 00:06:54,413
Undercover?

123
00:06:55,248 --> 00:06:56,331
I say that,

124
00:06:56,332 --> 00:07:00,085
but you'll just go as customers
and try on dresses.

125
00:07:00,086 --> 00:07:01,837
Mr. Himi and Ms. Asahi, can you manage?

126
00:07:01,838 --> 00:07:03,046
Yes.

127
00:07:03,047 --> 00:07:05,006
We are the engaged couple?

128
00:07:05,007 --> 00:07:06,883
Yeah. And Ms. Minamida,

129
00:07:06,884 --> 00:07:09,928
you and Funai
go talk to the bride and groom.

130
00:07:09,929 --> 00:07:11,097
Yes, understood.

131
00:07:14,100 --> 00:07:15,435
Could I go to the hotel

132
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:18,521
with Mr. Funai instead of Mr. Himi?

133
00:07:27,405 --> 00:07:28,780
KURASAWA

134
00:07:28,781 --> 00:07:30,490
Why did Ms. Asahi

135
00:07:30,491 --> 00:07:32,534
hate the idea of you being her fiancé?

136
00:07:32,535 --> 00:07:34,077
She didn't say she hated it.

137
00:07:34,078 --> 00:07:35,996
She just said she preferred Funai.

138
00:07:35,997 --> 00:07:37,832
I also wanted to go with Mr. Funai.

139
00:07:38,791 --> 00:07:39,750
Is that so?

140
00:07:40,251 --> 00:07:41,961
Well, I'm sorry about that.

141
00:07:43,629 --> 00:07:44,755
You are Ms. Hirono, right?

142
00:07:45,339 --> 00:07:47,340
We are here at your father's request.

143
00:07:47,341 --> 00:07:49,759
I'm Himi from Hirokawa & Howard LPC.

144
00:07:49,760 --> 00:07:51,094
It is a pleasure to meet you.

145
00:07:51,095 --> 00:07:52,555
Hello.

146
00:07:53,222 --> 00:07:54,473
Ms. Minamida...

147
00:07:54,474 --> 00:07:56,434
Please introduce yourself as well.

148
00:08:01,314 --> 00:08:03,356
It's a pleasure. I'm Minamida.

149
00:08:03,357 --> 00:08:05,109
ATTORNEY
MINAMI MINAMIDA

150
00:08:06,861 --> 00:08:07,819
Minami Minamida?

151
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,862
Yes!

152
00:08:08,863 --> 00:08:11,615
Read forwards or backwards,
it's Minami Minamida.

153
00:08:11,616 --> 00:08:14,826
Kayak, deed, rotator,
civic, racecar, Minami Minamida.

154
00:08:14,827 --> 00:08:15,744
What?

155
00:08:15,745 --> 00:08:17,914
I apologize.
She just joined the firm recently.

156
00:08:19,165 --> 00:08:20,625
- I see.
- Yes.

157
00:08:22,627 --> 00:08:24,085
Please have a seat.

158
00:08:24,086 --> 00:08:25,213
Thank you.

159
00:08:26,839 --> 00:08:28,758
Have you seen your husband since then?

160
00:08:29,467 --> 00:08:30,635
I haven't seen him.

161
00:08:31,802 --> 00:08:36,015
Actually, he told me he wants
to call off the marriage altogether.

162
00:08:37,266 --> 00:08:38,976
Is the dress incident the reason?

163
00:08:39,727 --> 00:08:42,145
I have a tattoo on my back.

164
00:08:42,146 --> 00:08:43,272
A tattoo?

165
00:08:48,319 --> 00:08:49,820
It's a magnolia, isn't it?

166
00:08:51,197 --> 00:08:53,615
It seems he couldn't accept the fact

167
00:08:53,616 --> 00:08:55,910
that the guests saw my tattoo.

168
00:08:57,078 --> 00:08:59,496
When did you notice
something was wrong with the dress?

169
00:08:59,497 --> 00:09:01,165
The morning of the wedding.

170
00:09:01,749 --> 00:09:04,251
<i>It fit perfectly at the fitting,</i>

171
00:09:04,252 --> 00:09:05,794
<i>but it was loose that day.</i>

172
00:09:05,795 --> 00:09:07,212
You must have lost weight.

173
00:09:07,213 --> 00:09:09,839
<i>I told the hotel staff, too,</i>

174
00:09:09,840 --> 00:09:11,842
<i>but they said
it was because I lost weight.</i>

175
00:09:12,468 --> 00:09:14,887
<i>So, I had them take the dress in.</i>

176
00:09:15,930 --> 00:09:19,058
Excuse me for asking,
but why did you rent your dress?

177
00:09:19,642 --> 00:09:21,017
I just assumed

178
00:09:21,018 --> 00:09:23,688
the Kurasawa family would naturally go
for a custom-made dress.

179
00:09:25,147 --> 00:09:28,442
I didn't invite anyone I know
to the wedding.

180
00:09:29,026 --> 00:09:29,859
Not one person?

181
00:09:29,860 --> 00:09:31,444
My father organized the wedding,

182
00:09:31,445 --> 00:09:33,739
so the guests
were all just his acquaintances.

183
00:09:34,615 --> 00:09:37,325
That's why I didn't particularly care.

184
00:09:37,326 --> 00:09:38,995
I see.

185
00:09:40,162 --> 00:09:42,373
Ms. Minamida,
is there anything you'd like to ask?

186
00:09:42,957 --> 00:09:43,791
Yes, there is.

187
00:09:45,501 --> 00:09:48,295
Ms. Hirono, do you love your husband?

188
00:09:48,296 --> 00:09:49,629
What?

189
00:09:49,630 --> 00:09:50,922
Why ask that out of nowhere?

190
00:09:50,923 --> 00:09:53,883
Even if you couldn't show it
to your friends,

191
00:09:53,884 --> 00:09:58,681
wouldn't you want your husband
to see you in a dress you cared about?

192
00:10:01,183 --> 00:10:03,143
Congratulations on your
Coming of Age, Ririi!

193
00:10:03,144 --> 00:10:04,519
The kimono looks great on you.

194
00:10:04,520 --> 00:10:05,645
Where's Minami?

195
00:10:05,646 --> 00:10:06,646
MINAMI'S DAD
MAKOTO

196
00:10:06,647 --> 00:10:07,940
Well...

197
00:10:10,943 --> 00:10:13,153
You're not wearing a kimono?

198
00:10:13,154 --> 00:10:15,655
It felt like a kelp roll,
and it was too uncomfortable.

199
00:10:15,656 --> 00:10:18,617
You put so much thought into that outfit.

200
00:10:18,618 --> 00:10:21,245
Don't you want to show it off
at least a little?

201
00:10:21,954 --> 00:10:23,956
That's what my father said.

202
00:10:25,082 --> 00:10:27,209
I apologize for her sudden, rude question.

203
00:10:33,507 --> 00:10:35,134
- Something wrong with the dress?
- Yes.

204
00:10:35,718 --> 00:10:38,303
Ms. Hirono said she felt it.
Did you know about it?

205
00:10:38,304 --> 00:10:40,180
No, I didn't know.

206
00:10:40,181 --> 00:10:41,265
I see.

207
00:10:42,183 --> 00:10:45,268
By the way, why do you want
to call off the marriage?

208
00:10:45,269 --> 00:10:46,394
Do I have to answer?

209
00:10:46,395 --> 00:10:47,687
No.

210
00:10:47,688 --> 00:10:50,649
Ms. Hirono said the tattoo
on her back was the reason.

211
00:10:50,650 --> 00:10:51,692
Hey...

212
00:10:53,402 --> 00:10:55,613
Yes. That's right.

213
00:10:56,155 --> 00:10:58,783
I knew about the tattoo
before the wedding.

214
00:10:59,408 --> 00:11:01,661
She got it on a whim when she was young,

215
00:11:02,161 --> 00:11:04,204
and I told her I didn't mind.

216
00:11:04,205 --> 00:11:05,121
Then why...

217
00:11:05,122 --> 00:11:08,375
Other people knowing about it
is a different story.

218
00:11:08,376 --> 00:11:10,543
My family and business partners

219
00:11:10,544 --> 00:11:13,964
won't necessarily be so accepting of it.

220
00:11:14,632 --> 00:11:17,259
Luckily, we haven't filed
our marriage papers yet.

221
00:11:25,434 --> 00:11:26,351
Are we done?

222
00:11:26,352 --> 00:11:29,063
I have my next meeting soon.

223
00:11:31,107 --> 00:11:32,650
Can I ask a question, too?

224
00:11:33,234 --> 00:11:34,776
- Go ahead.
- Are you sure?

225
00:11:34,777 --> 00:11:35,820
Yes.

226
00:11:37,279 --> 00:11:38,697
Do you love your wif--

227
00:11:41,158 --> 00:11:44,744
Excuse us. We'll be leaving now.
Ms. Minamida, let's go.

228
00:11:44,745 --> 00:11:47,372
Let's go. Come on.

229
00:11:47,373 --> 00:11:49,417
MIKOSHIBA LAND DEVELOPMENT

230
00:11:50,459 --> 00:11:54,213
Calling you "Mr. Funai"
would be weird, right?

231
00:11:55,256 --> 00:11:56,465
What do you mean?

232
00:11:57,258 --> 00:11:58,967
How we call each other.

233
00:11:58,968 --> 00:12:01,762
We're supposed to be engaged, after all.

234
00:12:03,389 --> 00:12:04,807
That's true.

235
00:12:05,474 --> 00:12:08,519
Then, shall we call each other
by our first names?

236
00:12:09,103 --> 00:12:10,521
Minato and Koharu.

237
00:12:13,983 --> 00:12:17,069
Wouldn't it sound more authentic
if we dropped the honorifics?

238
00:12:17,653 --> 00:12:19,113
Then... Koharu.

239
00:12:21,991 --> 00:12:23,159
Yes.

240
00:12:25,786 --> 00:12:28,746
Also, I thought up a backstory for us.

241
00:12:28,747 --> 00:12:29,706
Okay.

242
00:12:29,707 --> 00:12:31,666
We've been dating for six months.

243
00:12:31,667 --> 00:12:33,334
We met at the gym.

244
00:12:33,335 --> 00:12:36,129
We started talking
after seeing each other a lot.

245
00:12:36,130 --> 00:12:38,131
That sounds pretty realistic.

246
00:12:38,132 --> 00:12:40,175
The reason we're rushing the marriage

247
00:12:40,176 --> 00:12:43,845
is because a slightly impatient
little angel has come to us.

248
00:12:43,846 --> 00:12:44,762
A little angel?

249
00:12:44,763 --> 00:12:48,476
Minato... said we should do it
before my belly starts showing.

250
00:12:49,768 --> 00:12:52,270
I told him we didn't need a wedding, but...

251
00:12:52,271 --> 00:12:55,232
No way. I want to cherish
this milestone with you, Koharu.

252
00:12:56,150 --> 00:12:57,109
Okay.

253
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,907
ATTORNEY
TAKUMA HIMI

254
00:13:04,867 --> 00:13:05,910
Go ahead.

255
00:13:10,080 --> 00:13:10,914
Yes.

256
00:13:10,915 --> 00:13:14,125
We're done interviewing the bride
and groom, so I wanted to report back.

257
00:13:14,126 --> 00:13:16,377
<i>She said the dress felt off, too.</i>

258
00:13:16,378 --> 00:13:19,297
I see. Thank you.

259
00:13:19,298 --> 00:13:22,258
But rich families are such a pain.

260
00:13:22,259 --> 00:13:24,802
The bride is a puppet, and the groom

261
00:13:24,803 --> 00:13:28,556
- isn't committed. In this day and age...
<i>- Hirokawa & Howard LPC is on your side.</i>

262
00:13:28,557 --> 00:13:31,434
he's calling off the marriage
just over a tattoo.

263
00:13:31,435 --> 00:13:34,270
Mr. Himi, if this story
is going to take a while...

264
00:13:34,271 --> 00:13:36,523
<i>could you just send it in a message?</i>

265
00:13:36,524 --> 00:13:38,025
Thank you.

266
00:13:42,404 --> 00:13:43,363
Shall we go?

267
00:13:43,364 --> 00:13:44,406
Yes.

268
00:13:47,743 --> 00:13:50,204
Where did we leave off in our story?

269
00:13:50,913 --> 00:13:53,289
I was saying I want to cherish
our milestone.

270
00:13:53,290 --> 00:13:54,332
Right.

271
00:13:54,333 --> 00:13:56,377
And so, since we're doing this...

272
00:13:58,754 --> 00:14:00,422
It's my phone this time. Sorry.

273
00:14:01,382 --> 00:14:02,591
ATTORNEY
MINAMI MINAMIDA

274
00:14:03,175 --> 00:14:04,008
Yes, hello.

275
00:14:04,009 --> 00:14:06,052
Did you know that no human

276
00:14:06,053 --> 00:14:08,513
has ever seen a blue whale give birth?

277
00:14:08,514 --> 00:14:09,639
What?

278
00:14:09,640 --> 00:14:11,975
I thought I should share the whale talk

279
00:14:11,976 --> 00:14:14,227
I had planned
to tell you today, Mr. Funai.

280
00:14:14,228 --> 00:14:16,689
We haven't done that yet today, have we?

281
00:14:17,523 --> 00:14:19,858
It makes you wonder why,
considering a blue whale

282
00:14:19,859 --> 00:14:21,985
the size of an airplane
gives birth to a calf

283
00:14:21,986 --> 00:14:23,361
as heavy as a hippo, but...

284
00:14:23,362 --> 00:14:25,948
Hey... what are you talking about?

285
00:14:27,074 --> 00:14:28,409
<i>Ms. Asahi?</i>

286
00:14:28,993 --> 00:14:30,953
About a blue whale giving birth.

287
00:14:31,954 --> 00:14:34,498
<i>We're working,
so aren't you bothering him?</i>

288
00:14:37,126 --> 00:14:38,210
It's fine.

289
00:14:38,794 --> 00:14:41,505
Ms. Minamida, I'm busy now,
so I'll call you later.

290
00:14:42,089 --> 00:14:43,007
Okay.

291
00:14:44,925 --> 00:14:46,135
Is she always like this?

292
00:14:46,719 --> 00:14:48,762
Well... sometimes.

293
00:14:55,269 --> 00:14:56,312
Yes, hello.

294
00:14:57,313 --> 00:15:00,315
Did you know that fin whales
are migratory animals?

295
00:15:00,316 --> 00:15:01,482
What?

296
00:15:01,483 --> 00:15:04,569
And yet, a pod of 400 whales
living in the Gulf of California

297
00:15:04,570 --> 00:15:07,239
stays in the exact same spot
and refuses to move.

298
00:15:08,449 --> 00:15:10,868
Yes. Right now...

299
00:15:12,453 --> 00:15:13,495
Hello?

300
00:15:14,705 --> 00:15:16,206
Ms. Minamida?

301
00:15:18,083 --> 00:15:20,126
Whales feed deep in the ocean,

302
00:15:20,127 --> 00:15:21,670
then surface to defecate.

303
00:15:22,254 --> 00:15:23,129
You startled me...

304
00:15:23,130 --> 00:15:25,423
The reason blue whale feces is red

305
00:15:25,424 --> 00:15:27,467
is because their main diet, krill, is red.

306
00:15:27,468 --> 00:15:29,052
I see.

307
00:15:29,053 --> 00:15:32,389
How is that "sometimes"?
She is practically stalking you.

308
00:15:33,098 --> 00:15:34,474
I don't mind.

309
00:15:34,475 --> 00:15:36,225
I learn a lot,

310
00:15:36,226 --> 00:15:38,854
and besides,
I want to be there to listen to her.

311
00:15:43,233 --> 00:15:44,318
Can you...

312
00:15:44,860 --> 00:15:46,569
keep that up for the rest of your life?

313
00:15:46,570 --> 00:15:47,488
What?

314
00:15:48,364 --> 00:15:50,239
If you don't have that resolve,

315
00:15:50,240 --> 00:15:52,242
you should draw a line, Mr. Funai.

316
00:15:53,327 --> 00:15:56,372
Wouldn't that be what is best for her?

317
00:16:03,921 --> 00:16:05,254
Are you okay?

318
00:16:05,255 --> 00:16:07,216
What do you mean?

319
00:16:20,312 --> 00:16:21,355
Excuse me.

320
00:16:25,234 --> 00:16:27,611
It's definitely the boiled egg...

321
00:16:55,264 --> 00:16:57,182
Ms. Minamida, why are you here?

322
00:16:57,933 --> 00:16:59,517
I cannot say why I am here.

323
00:16:59,518 --> 00:17:02,062
Especially not to you, Mr. Funai.
Absolutely not.

324
00:17:04,815 --> 00:17:06,108
Where's Ms. Asahi?

325
00:17:12,031 --> 00:17:13,782
Ms. Asahi? I'm here.

326
00:17:14,742 --> 00:17:16,076
Over here! Give it to me!

327
00:17:21,832 --> 00:17:23,291
Hey, what is this?

328
00:17:23,292 --> 00:17:25,418
My suit pants were in my locker, right?

329
00:17:25,419 --> 00:17:26,503
They were.

330
00:17:27,004 --> 00:17:29,214
Then why did you bring this?

331
00:17:29,715 --> 00:17:31,633
It looked like
the easiest thing to put on.

332
00:17:33,302 --> 00:17:35,846
Give me a break...

333
00:17:41,018 --> 00:17:42,478
ASAHI

334
00:17:47,066 --> 00:17:48,484
Should I get you another outfit?

335
00:18:00,162 --> 00:18:01,455
Ms. Asahi?

336
00:18:02,539 --> 00:18:04,625
I'm done for.

337
00:18:06,085 --> 00:18:09,254
I yield this marriage to you.

338
00:18:11,048 --> 00:18:14,259
Take good care of... Minato.

339
00:18:22,643 --> 00:18:25,311
Please. If any dresses catch your eye,

340
00:18:25,312 --> 00:18:26,980
feel free to take it off the rack.

341
00:18:28,732 --> 00:18:29,858
Yes.

342
00:18:30,734 --> 00:18:32,568
We've been dating for six months.

343
00:18:32,569 --> 00:18:34,403
We met at the gym.

344
00:18:34,404 --> 00:18:36,489
We're rushing the wedding
because Ms. Asahi...

345
00:18:36,490 --> 00:18:39,993
I mean,
an impatient little angel in my belly.

346
00:18:41,453 --> 00:18:42,454
Is that so?

347
00:18:44,498 --> 00:18:48,460
This dress
would look great on you, Minami!

348
00:18:49,211 --> 00:18:51,087
It's very lovely.

349
00:18:51,088 --> 00:18:53,172
Would you like to try it on?

350
00:18:53,173 --> 00:18:56,343
Excuse me, about this dress...
I'm very sorry.

351
00:18:57,261 --> 00:18:58,804
Why is this out here?

352
00:19:08,647 --> 00:19:10,606
Is there a problem with that dress?

353
00:19:10,607 --> 00:19:11,649
No, honestly,

354
00:19:11,650 --> 00:19:15,403
that type of dress is out of fashion,
so we're swapping it out.

355
00:19:15,404 --> 00:19:17,822
You also have to be careful wearing it.

356
00:19:17,823 --> 00:19:19,157
You're right.

357
00:19:19,158 --> 00:19:20,908
Minami is petite.

358
00:19:20,909 --> 00:19:23,411
It'd be a disaster if it slipped down.

359
00:19:23,412 --> 00:19:24,787
Does that ever happen?

360
00:19:24,788 --> 00:19:26,455
That would never happen.

361
00:19:26,456 --> 00:19:28,375
We ensure the fitting is perfect.

362
00:19:29,376 --> 00:19:31,711
We have a design
that would look great on you,

363
00:19:31,712 --> 00:19:33,421
so I'll go prepare it.

364
00:19:33,422 --> 00:19:35,257
Right this way to the fitting room.

365
00:19:44,516 --> 00:19:47,644
Sir! That area is for employees only.

366
00:19:48,604 --> 00:19:50,021
- Is that so?
- Yes.

367
00:19:50,022 --> 00:19:51,106
I'm sorry.

368
00:19:57,821 --> 00:20:00,365
Hello, Ms. Asahi, are you okay now?

369
00:20:01,658 --> 00:20:04,077
So she's carrying a white dress.

370
00:20:04,786 --> 00:20:06,121
I'll try to find her.

371
00:20:39,863 --> 00:20:41,323
I just can't do it...!

372
00:20:42,658 --> 00:20:44,993
KOHARU ASAHI:
I'M SORRY! I COULDN'T DO IT!

373
00:20:47,454 --> 00:20:50,457
Sir, the bride has finished changing.

374
00:20:51,375 --> 00:20:52,459
Okay.

375
00:21:21,571 --> 00:21:23,031
How does it feel?

376
00:21:24,199 --> 00:21:26,033
I feel like a cabbage roll.

377
00:21:26,034 --> 00:21:27,286
It's so uncomfortable.

378
00:21:29,121 --> 00:21:32,332
My, my.
The groom is completely captivated.

379
00:21:34,167 --> 00:21:35,502
Are you captivated?

380
00:21:39,631 --> 00:21:40,756
CREATIVE RICE BALLS

381
00:21:40,757 --> 00:21:42,718
- I'm home.
- Welcome back. You're late.

382
00:21:43,468 --> 00:21:45,511
The Minami Minamida set is ready.

383
00:21:45,512 --> 00:21:47,972
I'm doing the dishes,
so take your lunchbox out.

384
00:21:47,973 --> 00:21:49,224
Wash your hands first.

385
00:21:56,064 --> 00:21:58,150
I said take your lunchbox out.

386
00:22:05,532 --> 00:22:06,616
What's this?

387
00:22:14,124 --> 00:22:16,751
"Special Maternity Wedding Plan"?

388
00:22:16,752 --> 00:22:18,003
What?

389
00:22:19,379 --> 00:22:22,298
What? No... Hey, calm down.

390
00:22:22,299 --> 00:22:24,133
No. Minami, getting married?

391
00:22:24,134 --> 00:22:25,885
Maternity? No way!

392
00:22:25,886 --> 00:22:27,762
No! That's impossible!

393
00:22:27,763 --> 00:22:29,097
There's no way.

394
00:22:34,728 --> 00:22:36,353
Mr. Minamida, is Minami home?

395
00:22:36,354 --> 00:22:37,688
Welcome, Ririi.

396
00:22:37,689 --> 00:22:39,316
Minami is washing her hands.

397
00:22:41,485 --> 00:22:42,818
You're hungry, right?

398
00:22:42,819 --> 00:22:45,654
I'll make you
a prototype brown sugar <i>ohagi.</i>

399
00:22:45,655 --> 00:22:46,864
Brown sugar <i>ohagi?</i>

400
00:22:46,865 --> 00:22:48,658
Yes! Now, sit down.

401
00:22:51,369 --> 00:22:52,369
So...

402
00:22:52,370 --> 00:22:55,248
What kind of things
do you talk about with Minami lately?

403
00:22:56,249 --> 00:22:57,584
Do you girls talk about boys?

404
00:22:58,794 --> 00:23:00,002
Not really.

405
00:23:00,003 --> 00:23:01,713
Right. Not really.

406
00:23:03,215 --> 00:23:06,051
Hey, did you see this?
Minami sent it to me.

407
00:23:11,056 --> 00:23:13,183
Minami!

408
00:23:14,059 --> 00:23:15,309
<i>Minami to the Minamida!</i>

409
00:23:15,310 --> 00:23:16,645
<i>Ririi to the Madoka!</i>

410
00:23:21,566 --> 00:23:23,692
- By the way, Dad...
- I don't want to hear it!

411
00:23:23,693 --> 00:23:25,695
I'm not listening!

412
00:23:26,655 --> 00:23:28,198
I'm absolutely not listening!

413
00:23:30,325 --> 00:23:31,576
My lunchbox...

414
00:23:32,244 --> 00:23:34,204
- Enjoy your meal.
- Thank you.

415
00:23:37,249 --> 00:23:38,375
Minato?

416
00:23:39,126 --> 00:23:40,127
Yes.

417
00:23:42,379 --> 00:23:43,212
Minato.

418
00:23:43,213 --> 00:23:44,964
What is it?

419
00:23:44,965 --> 00:23:47,508
You are "Minato," Mr. Funai.

420
00:23:47,509 --> 00:23:49,469
Minato and Minami
are only one letter apart.

421
00:23:50,262 --> 00:23:51,972
Come to think of it, you're right.

422
00:23:52,889 --> 00:23:54,473
Your name is a palindrome,

423
00:23:54,474 --> 00:23:57,601
but in kanji,

424
00:23:57,602 --> 00:24:00,063
it's also symmetrical left to right.

425
00:24:00,814 --> 00:24:04,526
My dad named me
after a manga character, Minami Asakura.

426
00:24:06,486 --> 00:24:08,612
Your name, Minato,

427
00:24:08,613 --> 00:24:11,240
means a harbor
where ships set sail into the ocean.

428
00:24:11,241 --> 00:24:12,159
Yes.

429
00:24:13,076 --> 00:24:15,536
A harbor is a place
where you can go to meet whales.

430
00:24:15,537 --> 00:24:18,623
I feel like I might meet a whale
when I'm with you.

431
00:24:19,791 --> 00:24:20,750
I see.

432
00:24:22,794 --> 00:24:25,005
I like the name Minato.

433
00:24:28,008 --> 00:24:29,259
Thank you.

434
00:24:31,261 --> 00:24:36,057
Do you have anything
to talk to me about besides whales?

435
00:24:37,893 --> 00:24:38,727
I don't.

436
00:24:41,521 --> 00:24:42,564
I see.

437
00:24:43,398 --> 00:24:44,441
You don't.

438
00:24:53,950 --> 00:24:55,702
Hello. Are you heading to lunch?

439
00:24:56,703 --> 00:24:58,412
It's you two. Why are you here?

440
00:24:58,413 --> 00:24:59,955
We were lying in wait.

441
00:24:59,956 --> 00:25:02,291
We're actually from a law firm.

442
00:25:02,292 --> 00:25:03,501
PARALEGAL
MINATO FUNAI

443
00:25:04,169 --> 00:25:07,213
At the wedding on October 11th,
a dress slipped off, didn't it?

444
00:25:07,214 --> 00:25:09,215
We have some questions about that.

445
00:25:09,216 --> 00:25:11,635
Where did you take this dress?

446
00:25:12,677 --> 00:25:13,928
I don't know anything...

447
00:25:13,929 --> 00:25:15,888
If you're worried

448
00:25:15,889 --> 00:25:18,683
about any repercussions,
please be rest assured.

449
00:25:19,434 --> 00:25:22,354
Hirokawa & Howard LPC is on your side!

450
00:25:23,521 --> 00:25:24,481
On your side.

451
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:32,822
COURTHOUSE

452
00:25:34,449 --> 00:25:35,491
FIRST HEARING:
WITNESS EXAM

453
00:25:35,492 --> 00:25:37,034
Witness, I understand

454
00:25:37,035 --> 00:25:40,163
you helped fit Ms. Hirono's dress
on the day of the wedding.

455
00:25:40,747 --> 00:25:44,292
Do you remember what Ms. Hirono said
when she put the dress on?

456
00:25:45,293 --> 00:25:46,127
Yes.

457
00:25:47,504 --> 00:25:49,673
I feel like it's a little loose.

458
00:25:51,466 --> 00:25:53,218
You must have lost weight.

459
00:25:53,802 --> 00:25:57,012
It's common for brides
to diet and lose weight

460
00:25:57,013 --> 00:25:58,806
before the day of the wedding.

461
00:25:58,807 --> 00:26:03,352
Besides, this dressmaker is highly skilled
and has a good reputation,

462
00:26:03,353 --> 00:26:05,146
so I didn't think the dress was the cause.

463
00:26:06,106 --> 00:26:07,857
Do you still think so?

464
00:26:17,450 --> 00:26:19,202
Well? Do you still think so now?

465
00:26:22,872 --> 00:26:23,873
No.

466
00:26:26,584 --> 00:26:28,211
Why is that?

467
00:26:29,796 --> 00:26:31,880
After the wedding ended,

468
00:26:31,881 --> 00:26:34,676
I learned it had been swapped
with a different dress.

469
00:26:38,179 --> 00:26:40,222
Apparently, on the morning of the wedding,

470
00:26:40,223 --> 00:26:44,435
a new staff member tore the dress
we had prepared.

471
00:26:44,436 --> 00:26:46,395
What are you crying for!

472
00:26:46,396 --> 00:26:48,355
<i>They didn't have time to fix it,</i>

473
00:26:48,356 --> 00:26:52,526
<i>so they swapped it with
a slightly larger one of the same design.</i>

474
00:26:52,527 --> 00:26:56,823
In other words, the staff hid that fact
from Ms. Hirono, didn't they?

475
00:26:57,532 --> 00:27:01,911
The chief told me
I'd be fired if I leaked it outside.

476
00:27:03,872 --> 00:27:07,459
I'm so sorry for keeping this to myself.

477
00:27:12,881 --> 00:27:13,882
Nothing further.

478
00:27:22,640 --> 00:27:25,268
Plaintiff, have you been suffering
this whole time?

479
00:27:26,102 --> 00:27:26,936
What?

480
00:27:27,771 --> 00:27:28,604
Yes.

481
00:27:28,605 --> 00:27:32,775
Do you have a social media account
under the handle "Magnolia"?

482
00:27:32,776 --> 00:27:33,692
What?

483
00:27:33,693 --> 00:27:34,652
Please answer.

484
00:27:36,696 --> 00:27:37,530
Yes.

485
00:27:38,615 --> 00:27:39,448
Your Honor.

486
00:27:39,449 --> 00:27:41,950
I would like to submit
new evidence, if I may.

487
00:27:41,951 --> 00:27:43,328
What is this about?

488
00:27:44,746 --> 00:27:49,333
I found posts from an account
believed to be the plaintiff's,

489
00:27:49,334 --> 00:27:52,253
- and I just confirmed it's hers.
- Objection.

490
00:27:53,755 --> 00:27:56,882
I do not believe the plaintiff's
personal social media posts

491
00:27:56,883 --> 00:27:58,425
are relevant to this dispute.

492
00:27:58,426 --> 00:27:59,511
Objection overruled.

493
00:28:03,098 --> 00:28:07,726
These posts were made from this account
on or after October 11th,

494
00:28:07,727 --> 00:28:09,729
the day of the wedding.

495
00:28:12,357 --> 00:28:15,235
"He told me he wants to call off
the marriage altogether."

496
00:28:15,985 --> 00:28:18,113
"I find myself feeling relieved."

497
00:28:19,406 --> 00:28:21,866
"I won't have to go through
with a fake marriage."

498
00:28:22,534 --> 00:28:25,078
"I should be grateful
the wedding was ruined."

499
00:28:28,623 --> 00:28:32,376
Earlier, you admitted you had been
"suffering this whole time."

500
00:28:32,377 --> 00:28:35,838
Yet you're suing the hotel
for a massive 100 million yen

501
00:28:35,839 --> 00:28:38,257
in emotional distress damages.

502
00:28:38,258 --> 00:28:40,176
How do you really feel?

503
00:28:42,137 --> 00:28:43,596
What exactly was painful?

504
00:28:54,315 --> 00:28:56,067
If you don't tell us,

505
00:28:56,693 --> 00:28:59,279
we can't help you either.

506
00:29:05,285 --> 00:29:07,077
I originally met him

507
00:29:07,078 --> 00:29:09,664
through an arranged marriage
set up by our parents.

508
00:29:10,999 --> 00:29:12,917
He took a liking to me,

509
00:29:14,210 --> 00:29:16,421
and things just kept moving forward...

510
00:29:17,756 --> 00:29:19,965
Especially since my father was so eager.

511
00:29:19,966 --> 00:29:22,594
He'd enter
into the Mikoshiba family, after all.

512
00:29:23,178 --> 00:29:24,637
There was that,

513
00:29:25,305 --> 00:29:29,099
but I think what my father
was really happy about was the bonus.

514
00:29:29,100 --> 00:29:30,434
The bonus?

515
00:29:30,435 --> 00:29:32,728
During our families' first meeting,

516
00:29:32,729 --> 00:29:36,733
his grandfather said he would give me
a <i>500-tsubo</i> plot of land

517
00:29:37,358 --> 00:29:39,778
in Yokohama as a wedding gift.

518
00:29:40,904 --> 00:29:42,988
My father had even made plans

519
00:29:42,989 --> 00:29:44,991
for how to use that land.

520
00:29:46,910 --> 00:29:47,952
But honestly,

521
00:29:48,620 --> 00:29:52,122
part of me wondered
if this was really the right choice.

522
00:29:52,123 --> 00:29:54,375
So that's why you posted that
on social media.

523
00:29:55,084 --> 00:29:58,213
I know it was a stupid thing to do.

524
00:30:02,884 --> 00:30:04,593
HOTEL CLAIM: MINIMUM 100 MILLION

525
00:30:04,594 --> 00:30:06,094
DAMAGES
EMOTIONAL DISTRESS

526
00:30:06,095 --> 00:30:08,348
MINIMUM 100 MILLION

527
00:30:22,570 --> 00:30:24,905
Ms. Hirono, it is a good thing
there was a bonus!

528
00:30:24,906 --> 00:30:25,865
What?

529
00:30:26,741 --> 00:30:28,742
Damages are divided into two categories,

530
00:30:28,743 --> 00:30:31,579
general damages and special damages,
did you know that?

531
00:30:32,914 --> 00:30:34,791
Are you testing me?

532
00:30:36,709 --> 00:30:40,671
General damages are damages
that ordinarily arise.

533
00:30:40,672 --> 00:30:44,633
Special damages are damages that arise
from extraordinary circumstances.

534
00:30:44,634 --> 00:30:47,719
In this case, the wedding costs
fall under general damages,

535
00:30:47,720 --> 00:30:49,596
but they only amount to about 30 million,

536
00:30:49,597 --> 00:30:51,766
making it difficult to claim 100 million.

537
00:30:52,350 --> 00:30:54,226
However, in reality,
Ms. Hirono had a bonus,

538
00:30:54,227 --> 00:30:57,688
that is,
the special circumstance of the land gift.

539
00:30:57,689 --> 00:31:02,693
This makes the marriage conditional
on the promised gift of the land.

540
00:31:02,694 --> 00:31:04,945
If the dress hadn't slipped off
at the wedding,

541
00:31:04,946 --> 00:31:07,739
the groom wouldn't have
called off the marriage,

542
00:31:07,740 --> 00:31:10,242
and the land
would have been gifted as promised.

543
00:31:10,243 --> 00:31:13,412
If we claim the value of the land

544
00:31:13,413 --> 00:31:15,455
Ms. Hirono lost as special damages,

545
00:31:15,456 --> 00:31:18,000
we can demand a much larger
compensation payout.

546
00:31:18,001 --> 00:31:21,253
Best of all, we no longer need to fixate
on emotional distress damages.

547
00:31:21,254 --> 00:31:24,756
Whatever the cause of your
mental suffering was,

548
00:31:24,757 --> 00:31:27,050
it has nothing to do with special damages.

549
00:31:27,051 --> 00:31:29,762
By the way, do you know
the land's estimated value?

550
00:31:30,346 --> 00:31:32,557
My dad said something
like three billion yen.

551
00:31:35,393 --> 00:31:38,103
If we claim that three billion as damages,

552
00:31:38,104 --> 00:31:40,440
the other side
will likely offer a settlement.

553
00:31:41,107 --> 00:31:43,901
Ten percent of three billion
is 300 million.

554
00:31:43,902 --> 00:31:45,695
We can negotiate from there.

555
00:31:47,655 --> 00:31:52,535
First, we must confirm this strategy
with your father.

556
00:31:53,328 --> 00:31:55,370
- Mr. Himi, will you come with me?
- Yes.

557
00:31:55,371 --> 00:31:57,331
I'll try drafting the brief.

558
00:31:57,332 --> 00:31:58,875
Yeah. Excuse us.

559
00:32:00,877 --> 00:32:01,711
Thank you.

560
00:32:06,799 --> 00:32:08,593
It's okay. I'm sure it'll go well.

561
00:32:09,510 --> 00:32:10,929
What do you mean, "go well"?

562
00:32:14,432 --> 00:32:18,227
My dress slipped down
and my wedding was ruined, right?

563
00:32:19,103 --> 00:32:21,813
What good would it do to demand money

564
00:32:21,814 --> 00:32:23,357
just because we're upset

565
00:32:23,358 --> 00:32:25,193
about not getting the land?

566
00:32:26,194 --> 00:32:28,904
- But the hotel was negligent--
- Did I--

567
00:32:28,905 --> 00:32:31,324
Did I ever say I wanted money?

568
00:32:32,450 --> 00:32:34,076
It's my case.

569
00:32:34,077 --> 00:32:35,662
It's my wedding.

570
00:32:36,245 --> 00:32:38,206
But nobody cares about me!

571
00:32:38,998 --> 00:32:41,542
Everyone only cares about my father.

572
00:32:43,836 --> 00:32:47,215
Is it difficult to tell your father
how you feel?

573
00:32:49,592 --> 00:32:51,885
How am I supposed to talk to someone

574
00:32:51,886 --> 00:32:53,721
who won't even lend an ear?

575
00:32:55,348 --> 00:32:58,017
I've given up on everything,

576
00:32:58,518 --> 00:33:00,353
from college to jobs.

577
00:33:03,856 --> 00:33:05,190
It's fine.

578
00:33:05,191 --> 00:33:08,987
I can't leave my parents anyway.

579
00:33:14,242 --> 00:33:15,702
I'm going home.

580
00:33:30,216 --> 00:33:31,884
HOW LONG WILL I KEEP RUNNING AWAY?

581
00:33:43,229 --> 00:33:44,772
Minami, you're home.

582
00:33:45,815 --> 00:33:48,358
Dad, if you could get a lot of money

583
00:33:48,359 --> 00:33:50,610
from the person I marry,
would you be happy?

584
00:33:50,611 --> 00:33:51,863
What?

585
00:33:52,655 --> 00:33:53,530
Why all of a sudden?

586
00:33:53,531 --> 00:33:54,782
- Would you be happy?
- Hold on.

587
00:33:55,450 --> 00:33:56,367
Hold on.

588
00:33:57,910 --> 00:34:01,539
Before talking about money,
you have something to tell me, right?

589
00:34:02,623 --> 00:34:05,459
I found someone who will listen to me
talk about whales,

590
00:34:05,460 --> 00:34:07,462
so I don't need to tell you.

591
00:34:09,380 --> 00:34:10,423
I see.

592
00:34:11,382 --> 00:34:14,135
You found someone like that.

593
00:34:24,771 --> 00:34:25,772
Listen, Minami.

594
00:34:26,814 --> 00:34:28,315
More than money,

595
00:34:28,316 --> 00:34:29,858
I'm worried about

596
00:34:29,859 --> 00:34:32,236
whether you'll be able to make it
on your own

597
00:34:32,820 --> 00:34:34,405
from now on.

598
00:34:35,406 --> 00:34:36,616
Okay.

599
00:34:37,200 --> 00:34:39,035
I don't know what kind of guy he is,

600
00:34:39,994 --> 00:34:42,037
but there's no guarantee

601
00:34:42,038 --> 00:34:44,415
he'll do things the same way I have.

602
00:34:46,292 --> 00:34:49,045
From now on,
you need to be able to prepare

603
00:34:49,712 --> 00:34:51,838
the Minami Minamida set yourself.

604
00:34:51,839 --> 00:34:52,840
By myself?

605
00:34:53,424 --> 00:34:54,967
Leaving your parents

606
00:34:55,968 --> 00:34:58,304
and becoming independent,
that is what it's all about.

607
00:34:59,806 --> 00:35:01,099
Independent adults

608
00:35:01,974 --> 00:35:04,519
prepare their own meals.

609
00:35:13,569 --> 00:35:15,195
Why are you crying, Dad?

610
00:35:15,196 --> 00:35:16,196
Be quiet.

611
00:35:16,197 --> 00:35:19,325
My head is a mess, so I don't know either!

612
00:35:21,953 --> 00:35:22,995
But Minami...

613
00:35:24,872 --> 00:35:25,957
congrats on your marriage.

614
00:35:28,251 --> 00:35:30,461
I'm getting married?

615
00:35:32,463 --> 00:35:33,381
What?

616
00:35:34,841 --> 00:35:35,758
You're not?

617
00:35:45,726 --> 00:35:47,686
300 million instead of 100 million.

618
00:35:47,687 --> 00:35:49,229
You really are different from MMK.

619
00:35:49,230 --> 00:35:50,897
We still have the witness exam.

620
00:35:50,898 --> 00:35:55,110
First, we must prove the hotel president
knew about the land gift.

621
00:35:55,111 --> 00:35:56,028
It's fine.

622
00:35:56,737 --> 00:35:59,782
He was there
at the families' meeting too. Right?

623
00:36:00,992 --> 00:36:01,826
Yeah.

624
00:36:02,326 --> 00:36:03,494
Then, right this way.

625
00:36:08,457 --> 00:36:09,584
Ms. Hirono.

626
00:36:14,338 --> 00:36:17,842
This is the very first
salted rice ball I've ever made.

627
00:36:18,843 --> 00:36:20,052
Please have it, if you'd like.

628
00:36:28,436 --> 00:36:32,023
Ms. Hirono, have you ever
prepared your own meals?

629
00:36:32,815 --> 00:36:34,525
I never had.

630
00:36:35,902 --> 00:36:36,903
Why do you ask that?

631
00:36:38,029 --> 00:36:40,155
My father told me that

632
00:36:40,156 --> 00:36:43,033
all independent adults
prepare their own meals.

633
00:36:43,034 --> 00:36:45,744
I prepared my meal, so today,

634
00:36:45,745 --> 00:36:48,664
I became independent from my father.

635
00:36:49,832 --> 00:36:53,085
I hope you can become independent
from your father, too.

636
00:36:58,633 --> 00:36:59,633
2ND HEARING:
WITNESS EXAM

637
00:36:59,634 --> 00:37:01,552
A wedding gift, you say?

638
00:37:02,094 --> 00:37:03,595
The groom's grandfather

639
00:37:03,596 --> 00:37:07,390
said he would give the plaintiff
a <i>500-tsubo</i> plot of land in Yokohama,

640
00:37:07,391 --> 00:37:10,686
and I hear you praised him,
saying, "How generous."

641
00:37:12,688 --> 00:37:14,856
I was merely stating a fact.

642
00:37:14,857 --> 00:37:15,900
So,

643
00:37:16,484 --> 00:37:20,570
you knew the groom's grandfather
promised the plaintiff

644
00:37:20,571 --> 00:37:24,533
land worth billions as a wedding gift?

645
00:37:26,535 --> 00:37:27,536
Yes.

646
00:37:29,497 --> 00:37:30,373
Thank you.

647
00:37:34,126 --> 00:37:35,543
Your Honor.

648
00:37:35,544 --> 00:37:38,505
The plaintiff had a special circumstance
where land would be gifted

649
00:37:38,506 --> 00:37:41,424
on the condition of marriage,
and the defendant was aware of it.

650
00:37:41,425 --> 00:37:43,760
Therefore, the plaintiff claims

651
00:37:43,761 --> 00:37:48,015
3.3 billion yen in damages
for the land she would've obtained.

652
00:37:49,767 --> 00:37:52,769
Please allow us to amend the claim
and cause of action.

653
00:37:52,770 --> 00:37:54,896
I see no reason to deny it.

654
00:37:54,897 --> 00:37:57,190
Please submit the motion to amend.

655
00:37:57,191 --> 00:37:58,109
Yes.

656
00:38:00,820 --> 00:38:02,738
Is there anything else?

657
00:38:04,323 --> 00:38:05,283
Excuse me...

658
00:38:06,075 --> 00:38:07,410
What is it, plaintiff?

659
00:38:08,160 --> 00:38:10,245
I want to drop the lawsuit.

660
00:38:10,246 --> 00:38:11,289
What?

661
00:38:15,042 --> 00:38:17,211
I'm dropping the lawsuit!

662
00:38:34,729 --> 00:38:36,147
How do I stop it?

663
00:38:40,192 --> 00:38:43,321
How do I get the criminal charges dropped?

664
00:38:46,407 --> 00:38:48,576
"Criminal charges" are for criminal cases.

665
00:38:49,452 --> 00:38:53,039
In this case, you might want to ask
how to drop the lawsuit.

666
00:38:54,665 --> 00:38:57,877
How do I... drop the lawsuit?

667
00:38:59,086 --> 00:39:01,921
There are two ways to drop a lawsuit.

668
00:39:01,922 --> 00:39:03,174
The easier one, please.

669
00:39:04,133 --> 00:39:05,508
If you turn to the judge

670
00:39:05,509 --> 00:39:07,469
and say, "I'm dropping the lawsuit,"

671
00:39:07,470 --> 00:39:08,846
it will be dropped.

672
00:39:10,890 --> 00:39:11,807
Is that it?

673
00:39:12,516 --> 00:39:14,060
Yes, that's it.

674
00:39:15,603 --> 00:39:16,896
That's easy.

675
00:39:18,230 --> 00:39:19,189
Yes.

676
00:39:19,190 --> 00:39:21,567
It's easier than making
a salted rice ball.

677
00:39:25,237 --> 00:39:27,406
Why couldn't I do this sooner?

678
00:39:28,991 --> 00:39:30,117
Are you an idiot?

679
00:39:30,701 --> 00:39:32,577
They just admitted
they knew about the land!

680
00:39:32,578 --> 00:39:35,498
The gallery will refrain
from making unsolicited remarks.

681
00:39:36,999 --> 00:39:38,125
Plaintiff.

682
00:39:40,169 --> 00:39:42,003
If you drop the lawsuit,

683
00:39:42,004 --> 00:39:45,882
the claim will be treated
as if it never existed. Are you sure?

684
00:39:45,883 --> 00:39:46,801
Yes.

685
00:39:48,052 --> 00:39:50,304
Defendant, do you consent?

686
00:39:50,888 --> 00:39:52,223
Yes, I consent.

687
00:39:54,475 --> 00:39:57,812
With the withdrawal of the lawsuit,
this case is concluded.

688
00:39:58,396 --> 00:39:59,480
Court is adjourned.

689
00:40:16,330 --> 00:40:18,374
Do you have any idea what you just did?

690
00:40:19,250 --> 00:40:20,583
This is...

691
00:40:20,584 --> 00:40:22,669
my case,

692
00:40:22,670 --> 00:40:24,546
my wedding,

693
00:40:24,547 --> 00:40:26,089
and my life!

694
00:40:26,090 --> 00:40:27,883
Don't get smart with me!

695
00:40:33,889 --> 00:40:35,014
You don't know

696
00:40:35,015 --> 00:40:38,351
a single thing
about my true feelings, Dad.

697
00:40:38,352 --> 00:40:39,895
There's no way you would.

698
00:40:40,855 --> 00:40:42,273
You haven't noticed a thing,

699
00:40:43,816 --> 00:40:45,650
even though we've been together

700
00:40:45,651 --> 00:40:47,611
for ten years.

701
00:41:03,544 --> 00:41:05,754
The magnolia flower

702
00:41:06,505 --> 00:41:07,882
on my back

703
00:41:08,674 --> 00:41:10,508
is to carve into my body

704
00:41:10,509 --> 00:41:12,636
my unwavering feelings for Hasumi.

705
00:41:19,727 --> 00:41:20,894
WEDDING PAYMENT DETAILS

706
00:41:20,895 --> 00:41:22,437
SENDER: HASUMI MIZUKI

707
00:41:22,438 --> 00:41:23,855
MAGNOLIA

708
00:41:23,856 --> 00:41:26,817
So that's why it was "Magnolia"...

709
00:41:27,401 --> 00:41:28,860
If I'm getting married,

710
00:41:28,861 --> 00:41:31,030
it's going to be with her.

711
00:41:31,697 --> 00:41:33,365
Because Hasumi

712
00:41:34,158 --> 00:41:35,910
is the one I love.

713
00:41:36,660 --> 00:41:39,079
Wow...

714
00:41:45,544 --> 00:41:46,670
Are you okay?

715
00:42:11,570 --> 00:42:12,863
Shinji Mikoshiba!

716
00:42:14,281 --> 00:42:15,490
What is it?

717
00:42:15,491 --> 00:42:17,243
The lawsuit was dropped, right?

718
00:42:17,993 --> 00:42:19,702
The lawsuit was dropped.

719
00:42:19,703 --> 00:42:21,622
But there's something bothering me.

720
00:42:23,749 --> 00:42:27,127
Do you love Hirono, Shinji?

721
00:42:30,089 --> 00:42:31,215
Why would you ask that?

722
00:42:32,258 --> 00:42:34,968
Because the lock screen on your smartphone

723
00:42:34,969 --> 00:42:37,221
is a photo of Hirono.

724
00:42:44,520 --> 00:42:45,687
Are we done?

725
00:42:45,688 --> 00:42:47,856
I have my next meeting soon.

726
00:42:49,858 --> 00:42:52,902
My friend told me
you'd normally hate to even look

727
00:42:52,903 --> 00:42:56,782
at the person
you're calling off a marriage with.

728
00:43:03,581 --> 00:43:04,831
I see!

729
00:43:04,832 --> 00:43:08,960
You realized Hirono liked someone else,

730
00:43:08,961 --> 00:43:11,380
so you called off the marriage
for her sake.

731
00:43:12,423 --> 00:43:14,091
If so, it all makes sense.

732
00:43:18,554 --> 00:43:20,097
You're overthinking it.

733
00:43:25,978 --> 00:43:27,646
I'm overthinking it?

734
00:43:29,231 --> 00:43:31,150
People's feelings are complicated.

735
00:43:37,281 --> 00:43:38,407
Ms. Minamida.

736
00:43:39,325 --> 00:43:40,158
Minato.

737
00:43:40,159 --> 00:43:42,786
We haven't had
our whale talk today yet, have we?

738
00:43:43,287 --> 00:43:45,122
Want to talk on the way back?

739
00:43:46,206 --> 00:43:47,041
Yes!

740
00:43:48,500 --> 00:43:51,712
But from now on, let's set a time to talk.

741
00:43:54,089 --> 00:43:55,049
Okay.

742
00:43:59,261 --> 00:44:01,387
Do you know about the humpback whale song?

743
00:44:01,388 --> 00:44:02,305
What?

744
00:44:02,306 --> 00:44:03,556
The humpback whale song is...

745
00:44:03,557 --> 00:44:07,101
I'm sorry we couldn't reach a settlement.

746
00:44:07,102 --> 00:44:08,770
It's more than enough.

747
00:44:08,771 --> 00:44:12,900
The Chairman highly evaluated our work.

748
00:44:13,734 --> 00:44:17,362
He says they're putting us
on retainer from now on.

749
00:44:17,363 --> 00:44:20,031
I see. That's good to hear.

750
00:44:20,032 --> 00:44:23,785
But the idea of special damages
was interesting.

751
00:44:23,786 --> 00:44:26,705
Ms. Minamida might become
an unexpected asset for us.

752
00:44:27,289 --> 00:44:28,207
"Unexpected"?

753
00:44:28,957 --> 00:44:30,500
Didn't you hire her, Managing Partner?

754
00:44:30,501 --> 00:44:32,126
What?

755
00:44:32,127 --> 00:44:33,753
Of course, I did.

756
00:44:33,754 --> 00:44:36,048
I just meant more than I expected.

757
00:44:44,598 --> 00:44:49,602
Subtitle translation by:
Hasan Hüseyin Öztürk

758
00:44:49,603 --> 00:44:50,561
NEXT EPISODE PREVIEW

759
00:44:50,562 --> 00:44:53,065
<i>The brother who committed
the assault is autistic.</i>

760
00:44:54,233 --> 00:44:55,650
If you want answers,

761
00:44:55,651 --> 00:44:57,860
try digging into what he likes.

762
00:44:57,861 --> 00:44:59,529
<i>Do I really have to do this?</i>

763
00:44:59,530 --> 00:45:01,448
Ultraman Zero!

764
00:45:04,326 --> 00:45:07,079
Shut up! You're autistic too, aren't you?

765
00:45:08,163 --> 00:45:10,790
It seems there's someone else
besides the defendant.

766
00:45:10,791 --> 00:45:12,708
<i>I can't be of any help to the defendant.</i>

767
00:45:12,709 --> 00:45:13,627
THIS DRAMA IS A WORK OF FICTION
